1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,680
This is Chip.

2
00:00:01,780 --> 00:00:03,280
Chip is a CPU.

3
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:07,860
A Ryzen 7 5800X3D, to be exact.

4
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:10,940
One of the best gaming processors ever made.

5
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:13,060
Chip has never cheated in his life.

6
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:14,040
Not once.

7
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:14,600
And yet…

8
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:15,720
Chip is banned.

9
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:17,080
Not an account.

10
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:17,880
Not a player.

11
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:19,000
The chip itself.

12
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,400
And the guy who paid for him?

13
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:22,600
Did absolutely nothing wrong.

14
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:25,460
This really happened, just a few weeks ago.

15
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,060
And by the end of this video,

16
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:29,380
you'll know why your next used PC part

17
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,200
might come with…

18
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,000
a criminal record.

19
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:34,900
Okay.

20
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:35,820
Meet Leo.

21
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:37,300
That's not his real name,

22
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,660
but he's a gamer in Germany,

23
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:40,740
and he just found a deal.

24
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:44,660
A used 5800X3D, on Kleinanzeigen.

25
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:48,120
Basically Germany's giant online flea market.

26
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:49,000
Good price.

27
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,280
Great chip.

28
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:52,040
What could possibly go wrong?

29
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:52,880
Spoiler.

30
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:53,480
Everything.

31
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:55,380
September twenty-first.

32
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:55,720
Chip arrives.

33
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:57,660
Leo installs him.

34
00:00:57,680 --> 00:00:58,820
Windows boots.

35
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,000
Everything works.

36
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:01,680
Leo opens Valorant…

37
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,000
…and the game kicks him out.

38
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:03,900
Instantly.

39
00:01:04,160 --> 00:01:06,560
So Leo does what every gamer does.

40
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:07,660
He restarts.

41
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:09,180
He updates his drivers.

42
00:01:09,420 --> 00:01:11,140
He reinstalls the game.

43
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:12,860
He turns it off and on again.

44
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:13,620
Kicked.

45
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:16,480
Leo puts his old CPU back in…

46
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,360
and Valorant works perfectly.

47
00:01:18,540 --> 00:01:19,240
Put Chip in?

48
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:19,880
Kicked.

49
00:01:19,900 --> 00:01:20,800
Take Chip out?

50
00:01:20,820 --> 00:01:21,520
Fine.

51
00:01:21,580 --> 00:01:23,560
So Leo writes to Riot support.

52
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,760
And the answer is a little terrifying.

53
00:01:25,991 --> 00:01:27,160
According to Leo,

54
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:29,980
support told him this exact processor had

55
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,400
been hardware banned on August twelfth.

56
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:34,320
That's more than a month before he even

57
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:35,300
bought it.

58
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:35,620
Chip…

59
00:01:35,620 --> 00:01:36,640
had a past.

60
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,400
Let's rewind.

61
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,940
Summer 2026.

62
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,480
Chip lived with a different owner.

63
00:01:41,500 --> 00:01:42,420
And that owner…

64
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:44,180
was not playing fair.

65
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,520
Cheats were detected.

66
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:46,760
Riot dropped the hammer.

67
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:49,300
And the ban didn't just hit an account.

68
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:50,100
It hit the hardware.

69
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,740
Including Chip.

70
00:01:51,886 --> 00:01:53,600
And then, the previous owner did the most

71
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,560
natural thing in the world.

72
00:01:55,660 --> 00:01:56,800
He sold it.

73
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:58,560
But wait.

74
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:00,620
How do you even ban a piece of silicon?

75
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:01,880
Chip doesn't have a name.

76
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:02,620
Or an email.

77
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,920
Or a face.

78
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:04,380
Well…

79
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,520
this one does.

80
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,980
To understand this, you need to meet Vanguard.

81
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:09,780
Riot's anti-cheat.

82
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:11,500
Vanguard doesn't live in some normal

83
00:02:11,520 --> 00:02:13,060
corner of your PC.

84
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:15,760
It runs in the kernel, the deepest and

85
00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,600
most powerful layer of your system,

86
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:20,560
and it starts the moment your computer boots.

87
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:21,960
Before your desktop.

88
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:23,560
Before your wallpaper.

89
00:02:23,660 --> 00:02:24,620
Before you.

90
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:26,600
Think of Valorant as a club,

91
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,640
and Vanguard as the bouncer who never

92
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:30,060
forgets a face.

93
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:32,060
But computers don't have faces.

94
00:02:32,260 --> 00:02:34,700
So what does the bouncer actually remember?

95
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:36,260
Here's the clever part.

96
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:38,460
On Windows 11, Valorant needs something

97
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:41,060
called TPM 2.0.

98
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:44,760
A tiny security vault that stores secret keys.

99
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:47,900
And on AMD Ryzen chips, that vault isn't a

100
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,020
separate part.

101
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:51,480
It's built right inside the processor.

102
00:02:51,560 --> 00:02:53,180
So when you buy a used Ryzen,

103
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,000
you're not just buying a CPU.

104
00:02:55,500 --> 00:02:56,960
You're buying its vault.

105
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:57,900
Its keys.

106
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:58,900
Its identity.

107
00:02:59,060 --> 00:03:01,460
Riot hasn't said exactly what it reads.

108
00:03:01,600 --> 00:03:03,420
But experts suspect a unique key,

109
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:06,460
created inside that vault when the chip is made.

110
00:03:07,621 --> 00:03:08,754
Reinstall Windows?

111
00:03:08,774 --> 00:03:09,560
Same key.

112
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:10,366
New account?

113
00:03:10,386 --> 00:03:11,172
Same key.

114
00:03:11,192 --> 00:03:12,381
Brand-new game install?

115
00:03:12,401 --> 00:03:13,940
You guessed it.

116
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,840
Every time you launch Valorant,

117
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:17,660
Vanguard checks your hardware against

118
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:19,180
Riot's ban list.

119
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,680
And if a part matches a banned machine…

120
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,300
the door stays shut.

121
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:25,380
So to Vanguard, Chip isn't a CPU.

122
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:27,200
Chip is that guy.

123
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:29,220
But here's the plot twist.

124
00:03:29,380 --> 00:03:30,720
Riot's head of anti-cheat,

125
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:33,640
Phillip Koskinas, says parts of this story

126
00:03:33,660 --> 00:03:35,140
don't add up.

127
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:36,820
He says he couldn't find a support ticket

128
00:03:36,840 --> 00:03:39,160
that matches Leo's, and he called the

129
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,980
whole thing pretty unlikely.

130
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,680
Leo also says his motherboard and his SSD

131
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:45,460
got flagged too.

132
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,060
Riot says no.

133
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:49,120
When one part matches, it doesn't

134
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,380
blacklist everything else in your PC.

135
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:53,120
So who's telling the truth?

136
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:53,840
Honestly…

137
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:55,320
we don't fully know yet.

138
00:03:55,340 --> 00:03:57,660
But Riot did confirm two things.

139
00:03:57,900 --> 00:04:00,220
One, its hardware bans last four months,

140
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:01,180
at most.

141
00:04:01,500 --> 00:04:03,660
Two, they only apply to the game where the

142
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,900
cheating happened.

143
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:07,620
So if Chip was banned on August twelfth…

144
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:09,500
his sentence should end around the middle

145
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:10,460
of December.

146
00:04:10,760 --> 00:04:12,960
And that's the part that actually hurts.

147
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,140
You save up.

148
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,780
You hunt for a good deal.

149
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,940
You build your setup piece by piece…

150
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:21,020
and you end up paying for someone else's mistake.

151
00:04:21,060 --> 00:04:22,300
And the worst part?

152
00:04:22,320 --> 00:04:24,180
The system did exactly what it was built

153
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,040
to do.

154
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:25,360
Just…

155
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:26,960
to the wrong person.

156
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:29,220
And right now, there's no real way to

157
00:04:29,240 --> 00:04:32,660
check a used CPU for a ban before you buy it.

158
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:34,760
So here's how to protect yourself.

159
00:04:34,820 --> 00:04:35,120
One.

160
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:37,120
Buy from a seller or a marketplace with a

161
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:37,740
return window.

162
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:39,060
Two.

163
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:41,200
The day it arrives, test it in every game

164
00:04:41,220 --> 00:04:42,470
you play with anti-cheat.

165
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:43,660
Three.

166
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:46,300
Keep the receipt and your chat with the seller.

167
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,060
And four.

168
00:04:47,080 --> 00:04:49,780
If you get hit, contact the game's support.

169
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:51,960
Riot says they'll tell you how long the

170
00:04:51,980 --> 00:04:53,100
ban has left.

171
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,000
Because some anti-cheat systems give

172
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:56,840
temporary hardware bans…

173
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,120
and some don't.

174
00:04:58,140 --> 00:04:59,180
As for Chip?

175
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:00,440
He's not a cheater.

176
00:05:00,460 --> 00:05:02,360
He just had a really bad roommate.

177
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:04,960
Somewhere in Germany, a little Ryzen is

178
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:07,460
counting down the days until December.

179
00:05:07,583 --> 00:05:09,300
So tell me in the comments.

180
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:12,400
Would you ever buy a used CPU again?

181
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,300
And subscribe, because next time,

182
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:16,480
we're finding out what else your hardware

183
00:05:16,500 --> 00:05:18,860
secretly remembers about you.

184
00:05:18,880 --> 00:05:19,880
See you, Chip.
